\ kstack.4 - the stack check, calling its error's message only when there is
\ something to say (Iteration 116, the gene kstack). The interpreter runs
\ ?STACK after every word, and the kernel's - DEPTH DUP 0< SWAP 10000 > OR
\ ABORT" Stack error" - called (ABORT") every time, only to skip the message.
\ This is the kernel input gene's own ?STACK8 (cv8b-kinput.4, Iteration 54)
\ on its own, for designs without that gene's C code: one unsigned compare
\ (DEPTH's logical shift makes an underflow huge), behind an IF. The same
\ check, message and WARM on failure. The converter swaps ?STACK8's body
\ into ?STACK, so INTERPRET's call reaches it.

: ?STACK8 ( --- )
  DEPTH 10000 U> IF -1 ABORT" Stack error" THEN ;
